<section class="lf-guide-faq">
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <details><summary>How do you market a Christmas light installation business?</summary><p>Combine relevant local search visibility, paid search, visual social advertising, real project proof, a dedicated quote funnel and reliable follow-up.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is Google Ads or Facebook Ads better for Christmas light installers?</summary><p>Google Search Ads can capture active installation searches, while Facebook and Instagram ads can introduce the service visually. The best mix depends on local demand, creative, budget and lead quality.</p></details>
<details><summary>When should installers start Christmas lighting marketing?</summary><p>Plan ahead of peak demand, with timing based on the local season, returning customers, commercial buying cycles and crew availability.</p></details>
<details><summary>What should a Christmas lighting lead form ask?</summary><p>Typically property location, type, installation scope, approximate budget and preferred next step, tailored to the business&#x27;s actual process.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do I need a Christmas lighting marketing agency?</summary><p>Not necessarily. An installer can manage campaigns internally or hire specialists for advertising, conversion funnels, CRM and reporting.</p></details>
